Claude (via proxy) for Home Assistant

This project is a modified copy of the `anthropic` integration from Home
Assistant Core (https://github.com/home-assistant/core), Copyright Home
Assistant contributors, licensed under the Apache License, Version 2.0.

The files under custom_components/claude_proxy/ and tests/ come from
homeassistant/components/anthropic/ and tests/components/anthropic/ at the
release recorded in the UPSTREAM file. Changes from that release:

- The integration domain is `claude_proxy`, so it can run alongside the core
  integration, and import paths point to `custom_components.claude_proxy`.
- The config flow asks for a proxy base URL, which is passed to the Anthropic
  SDK client.
- proxy.py and model_capabilities.json fill in model metadata (lifecycle and
  capabilities) that proxies leave out of `GET /v1/models`.
- Translations are resolved into translations/en.json, and user-facing text is
  reworded for proxy setups.

The full set of changes is the git diff between the `upstream` and `main`
branches of this repository.

